{"id":"mahabharata-6-047","work":"mahabharata","part":6,"partName":"भीष्मपर्व","partNameEn":"Bhishma Parva","unit":47,"title":"सप्तचत्वारिंशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 47 · Second day: the two formations","summary":{"en":"Duryodhana sees the Pandava Krauncha array and tells Drona, Kripa and the others to guard Bhishma. The Kaurava leaders take their positions and conches and drums sound.","kn":"ಪಾಂಡವರ ಕ್ರೌಂಚವ್ಯೂಹ ನೋಡಿದ ದುರ್ಯೋಧನನು ಭೀಷ್ಮನನ್ನು ರಕ್ಷಿಸುವಂತೆ ದ್ರೋಣ, ಕೃಪಾದಿಗಳಿಗೆ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಕೌರವ ನಾಯಕರು ಸ್ಥಾನ ಹಿಡಿಯುತ್ತಾರೆ, ಶಂಖ ಭೇರಿಗಳು ಮೊಳಗುತ್ತವೆ.","hi":"पाण्डवों का क्रौंच व्यूह देखकर दुर्योधन द्रोण, कृप आदि से भीष्म की रक्षा करने को कहता है। कौरव नायक अपने स्थान लेते हैं और शंख-नगाड़े बजते हैं।","te":"పాండవుల క్రౌంచ వ్యూహాన్ని చూసి దుర్యోధనుడు భీష్ముని కాపాడమని ద్రోణ, కృపాదులకు చెబుతాడు. కౌరవ నాయకులు స్థానాలు తీసుకుంటారు, శంఖాలు భేరీలు మోగుతాయి.","ta":"பாண்டவரின் கிரௌஞ்ச வியூகத்தைக் கண்ட துரியோதனன் பீஷ்மரைக் காக்கும்படி த்ரோணர், கிருபர் முதலியோரிடம் கூறுகிறான். கௌரவத் தலைவர்கள் இடம் பிடிக்க, சங்கும் முரசும் முழங்குகின்றன.","ml":"പാണ്ഡവരുടെ ക്രൗഞ്ച വ്യൂഹം കണ്ട ദുര്യോധനൻ ഭീഷ്മരെ സംരക്ഷിക്കാൻ ദ്രോണർ, കൃപർ മറ്റുള്ളവരോട് ആവശ്യപ്പെടുന്നു. കൗരവ നേതാക്കൾ സ്ഥാനമുറപ്പിക്കുന്നു; ശംഖും ഭേരിയും മുഴങ്ങുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 6.47; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Jul 26 2021","sections":[{"title":"भीष्मवधपर्व","titleEn":"Bhishmavadha Parva (The fall of Bhishma)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"क्रौञ्चं ततो महाव्यूहमभेद्यं तनयस्तव ।\nव्यूढं दृष्ट्वा महाघोरं पार्थेनामिततेजसा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then your son, seeing the great, dreadful and impenetrable Krauncha formation arrayed by the boundlessly radiant Partha,"}},{"n":2,"text":"आचार्यमुपसंगम्य कृपं शल्यं च मारिष ।\nसौमदत्तिं विकर्णं च अश्वत्थामानमेव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"went to the teacher Drona, and to Kripa, Shalya, Somadatta's son, Vikarna and Ashvatthama, sir,"}},{"n":3,"text":"दुःशासनादीन्भ्रातॄंश्च स सर्वानेव भारत ।\nअन्यांश्च सुबहूञ्शूरान्युद्धाय समुपागतान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"and to his brothers led by Duhshasana, and to many other heroes who had come to fight."}},{"n":4,"text":"प्राहेदं वचनं काले हर्षयंस्तनयस्तव ।\nनानाशस्त्रप्रहरणाः सर्वे शस्त्रास्त्रवेदिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"At that moment your son, gladdening them, said these words: \"All of you wield various weapons and know weapons and missiles.\""}},{"n":5,"text":"एकैकशः समर्था हि यूयं सर्वे महारथाः ।\nपाण्डुपुत्रान्रणे हन्तुं ससैन्यान्किमु संहताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Each of you great chariot-warriors alone is able to kill the sons of Pandu with their army in battle; how much more together!\""}},{"n":6,"text":"अपर्याप्तं तदस्माकं बलं भीष्माभिरक्षितम् ।\nपर्याप्तं त्विदमेतेषां बलं पार्थिवसत्तमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"That army of ours, guarded by Bhishma, is insufficient; but this army of theirs, best of kings, is sufficient.\""}},{"n":7,"text":"संस्थानाः शूरसेनाश्च वेणिकाः कुकुरास्तथा ।\nआरेवकास्त्रिगर्ताश्च मद्रका यवनास्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Let the Samsthanas, Shurasenas, Venikas, Kukuras, Arevakas, Trigartas, Madrakas and Yavanas,\""}},{"n":8,"text":"शत्रुंजयेन सहितास्तथा दुःशासनेन च ।\nविकर्णेन च वीरेण तथा नन्दोपनन्दकैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"with Shatrunjaya, Duhshasana, the hero Vikarna, and Nanda and Upananda,\""}},{"n":9,"text":"चित्रसेनेन सहिताः सहिताः पाणिभद्रकैः ।\nभीष्ममेवाभिरक्षन्तु सह सैन्यपुरस्कृताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"with Chitrasena and the Panibhadrakas, put the army ahead of them and guard Bhishma alone.\""}},{"n":10,"text":"ततो द्रोणश्च भीष्मश्च तव पुत्रश्च मारिष ।\nअव्यूहन्त महाव्यूहं पाण्डूनां प्रतिबाधने ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Drona, Bhishma and your son arrayed a great formation to resist the Pandavas."}},{"n":11,"text":"भीष्मः सैन्येन महता समन्तात्परिवारितः ।\nययौ प्रकर्षन्महतीं वाहिनीं सुरराडिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Surrounded on every side by a great army, Bhishma went forward, leading the huge host like the king of the gods."}},{"n":12,"text":"तमन्वयान्महेष्वासो भारद्वाजः प्रतापवान् ।\nकुन्तलैश्च दशार्णैश्च मागधैश्च विशां पते ॥","meaning":{"en":"The mighty archer Drona, son of Bharadvaja, full of power, followed him, with the Kuntalas, Dasharnas and Magadhas, lord of the people,"}},{"n":13,"text":"विदर्भैर्मेकलैश्चैव कर्णप्रावरणैरपि ।\nसहिताः सर्वसैन्येन भीष्ममाहवशोभिनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"the Vidarbhas, Mekalas and Karnapravaranas, together with all their forces, following Bhishma who shone in battle."}},{"n":14,"text":"गान्धाराः सिन्धुसौवीराः शिबयोऽथ वसातयः ।\nशकुनिश्च स्वसैन्येन भारद्वाजमपालयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Gandharas, Sindhus, Sauviras, Shibis and Vasatis, and Shakuni with his own army, guarded Drona."}},{"n":15,"text":"ततो दुर्योधनो राजा सहितः सर्वसोदरैः ।\nअश्वातकैर्विकर्णैश्च तथा शर्मिलकोसलैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then King Duryodhana, with all his brothers, with the Ashvatakas, Vikarnas, Sharmilas and Kosalas,"}},{"n":16,"text":"दरदैश्चूचुपैश्चैव तथा क्षुद्रकमालवैः ।\nअभ्यरक्षत संहृष्टः सौबलेयस्य वाहिनीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"the Daradas, Chuchupas, Kshudrakas and Malavas, gladly guarded the army of Subala's son."}},{"n":17,"text":"भूरिश्रवाः शलः शल्यो भगदत्तश्च मारिष ।\nविन्दानुविन्दावावन्त्यौ वामं पार्श्वमपालयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhurishravas, Shala, Shalya and Bhagadatta, sir, and the two Avantis, Vinda and Anuvinda, guarded the left side."}},{"n":18,"text":"सौमदत्तिः सुशर्मा च काम्बोजश्च सुदक्षिणः ।\nशतायुश्च श्रुतायुश्च दक्षिणं पार्श्वमास्थिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Somadatta's son, Susharma, Sudakshina the Kamboja, Shatayu and Shrutayu stood on the right side."}},{"n":19,"text":"अश्वत्थामा कृपश्चैव कृतवर्मा च सात्वतः ।\nमहत्या सेनया सार्धं सेनापृष्ठे व्यवस्थिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ashvatthama, Kripa and the Satvata Kritavarman stood at the rear of the army with a large force."}},{"n":20,"text":"पृष्ठगोपास्तु तस्यासन्नानादेश्या जनेश्वराः ।\nकेतुमान्वसुदानश्च पुत्रः काश्यस्य चाभिभूः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The protectors of its rear were kings of various countries: Ketuman, Vasudana, and Abhibhu, the son of the king of Kashi."}},{"n":21,"text":"ततस्ते तावकाः सर्वे हृष्टा युद्धाय भारत ।\nदध्मुः शङ्खान्मुदा युक्ताः सिंहनादांश्च नादयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then all your men, delighted, O Bharata, eager for battle, joyfully blew their conches and roared like lions."}},{"n":22,"text":"तेषां श्रुत्वा तु हृष्टानां कुरुवृद्धः पितामहः ।\nसिंहनादं विनद्योच्चैः शङ्खं दध्मौ प्रतापवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing their joy, the grandfather, the aged Kuru, mighty, roared a high lion's roar and blew his conch."}},{"n":23,"text":"ततः शङ्खाश्च भेर्यश्च पेश्यश्च विविधाः परैः ।\nआनकाश्चाभ्यहन्यन्त स शब्दस्तुमुलोऽभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then conches, kettledrums, tabors and drums of various kinds were struck by the enemy, and a tumultuous noise arose."}},{"n":24,"text":"ततः श्वेतैर्हयैर्युक्ते महति स्यन्दने स्थितौ ।\nप्रदध्मतुः शङ्खवरौ हेमरत्नपरिष्कृतौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the two standing in a great chariot yoked to white horses, adorned with gold and jewels, blew their excellent conches."}},{"n":25,"text":"पाञ्चजन्यं हृषीकेशो देवदत्तं धनंजयः ।\nपौण्ड्रं दध्मौ महाशङ्खं भीमकर्मा वृकोदरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hrishikesha blew Panchajanya, Dhananjaya Devadatta, and Vrikodara, of fearsome deeds, the great conch Paundra."}},{"n":26,"text":"अनन्तविजयं राजा कुन्तीपुत्रो युधिष्ठिरः ।\nनकुलः सहदेवश्च सुघोषमणिपुष्पकौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"King Yudhishthira, son of Kunti, blew Anantavijaya, and Nakula and Sahadeva blew Sughosha and Manipushpaka."}},{"n":27,"text":"काशिराजश्च शैब्यश्च शिखण्डी च महारथः ।\nधृष्टद्युम्नो विराटश्च सात्यकिश्च महायशाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king of Kashi, Shaibya, the great chariot-warrior Shikhandi, Dhrishtadyumna, Virata, and the very famous Satyaki,"}},{"n":28,"text":"पाञ्चाल्यश्च महेष्वासो द्रौपद्याः पञ्च चात्मजाः ।\nसर्वे दध्मुर्महाशङ्खान्सिंहनादांश्च नेदिरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"the great archer prince of Panchala, and the five sons of Draupadi, all blew their great conches and roared lion-roars."}},{"n":29,"text":"स घोषः सुमहांस्तत्र वीरैस्तैः समुदीरितः ।\nनभश्च पृथिवीं चैव तुमुलो व्यनुनादयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That great sound, raised there by those heroes, thunderously made the sky and the earth echo."}},{"n":30,"text":"एवमेते महाराज प्रहृष्टाः कुरुपाण्डवाः ।\nपुनर्युद्धाय संजग्मुस्तापयानाः परस्परम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So, great king, the Kurus and the Pandavas, delighted, came together again for battle, each tormenting the other."}}]}]}